{
  "_readme": [
    "AUDIO IDENTITY FOR THE 27 LONG-FORM PACKS — one file so a reviewer can read every pack's",
    "sound side by side, exactly as scripts/apply-audio-profiles.js's PROFILES table and",
    "film_skins/_metadata.json already do for the other two families.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. gen-lf-packs.js stamped every one of these packs from a NICHE_AUDIO table",
    "that only ever had a `default` key, through an audioFor() that took no argument. All 27",
    "shipped byte-identical: the same mood sentence, the same four genres, the same ten",
    "keywords. Night Shift and Allotment both asked the catalogue for warm acoustic folk, so",
    "every long-form film drew from one pool and they all sounded alike — the exact convergence",
    "the music vocabulary work fixed for the short packs and never reached this family.",
    "",
    "AUTHORING RULES, both enforced by npm test:",
    "  · style[] is emitted as the PHRASE *and* its component words, so a compound must itself",
    "    resolve to >= 3 tracks. Prefer single words; the compounds here are cache-verified.",
    "  · musicKeywords are split into words, so phrases are free — but each WORD must resolve.",
    "  · Two packs in one archetype may not declare the same genre set (test:music-diversity).",
    "Change a term here, then run `npm run audio:profiles` and `npm run test:music-vocab`."
  ],
